  "report": "Initial stage: packaging reception is positive across several distinct TikTok accounts in one brand-owned video thread. P00’s chic/environmentally friendly statement has 296 displayed likes; P15’s planned reuse of an empty container has 150. These show visible resonance, not verified experiences or purchase effects. Aesthetic approval recurs across distinct accounts, but environmental performance does not receive independent factual corroboration: P01 is brand agreement, P03 is P00’s own qualified explanation, and P02 questions recyclability. Packaging SKU/version is generally unknown; the supplied product catalog cannot resolve it.\n\nP06 alone reports arrival leakage with a loose top, opening and cleaning the product, and concern about oxygen exposure. This is one customer observation, with 12 likes, without independent corroboration in the supplied focal set. P07, the brand, says short exposure is not an issue and offers a replacement conditional on contacting support; this establishes an offer, not shipment, delivery, or independently verified product safety. No supplied focal account reports a replacement sent or retailer leakage. Positive aesthetics and this functional failure coexist; approval does not rebut the complaint. No defect rate or verified causal mechanism follows.\n\nConsequences remain source-specific: P17 reports an all-Experiment routine and Continuum in transit, expressing loyalty without attributing it to packaging. P20 expresses broad buying enthusiasm without establishing completed checkout. P32 tentatively considers saving up; P38 intends to try; P42 reports receipt and newly discovered refillability. P04/P27 request refill bundles, P29 asks about a sticker in a refill, and P15 plans container reuse. None explicitly establishes future repeat purchase intent or packaging-caused purchase. P26 praises packaging while questioning skin benefits.\n\nAll focal observations were captured 2026-09-09T11:56:25.935Z; displayed publication dates omit the year. Raw likes are retained below; low counts lack enough exposure context to establish material resonance. Focal keys count source accounts/records as requested, not independent humans or events: P00/P03 share an actor, as do P01/P07. No context-only records were supplied. Coverage is bounded: 47 displayed bodies versus 72 advertised comments does not prove completeness; only selected reply branches were expanded, and native comment IDs are unavailable. A second-stage evidence set was not supplied, so second-stage findings and changes cannot be diagnosed. Counts below apply only to this initial focal set.",
  "source_index": [
    {
      "key": "P00",
      "findings": "@randomdude7551, TikTok, 5-15 (year unavailable): calls metal packaging chic and environmentally friendly; SKU/version unknown. 296 displayed likes support resonance of the combined statement, not verified environmental performance. Same actor as P03."
    },
    {
      "key": "P01",
      "findings": "@experimentwrld, brand/creator TikTok reply to P00, 5-15: agrees completely; 39 likes. Brand endorsement, not independent customer corroboration. Same actor as P07."
    },
    {
      "key": "P02",
      "findings": "@person1234567556987, TikTok reply to P00, 5-15: questions environmental friendliness and recyclability; 0 likes. Raises unresolved verification questions rather than demonstrating non-recyclability; SKU/version unknown."
    },
    {
      "key": "P03",
      "findings": "@randomdude7551, TikTok reply under P00, 5-15: says aluminum is almost always recyclable, inner part likely recyclable, pump likely not, and pump/shell reusable; 2 likes. Qualified assertions without verification; repeats P00's actor, not another origin."
    },
    {
      "key": "P04",
      "findings": "@flamingpanda5, TikTok reply under P00, 5-20: requests refill bundles; 0 likes. Product unspecified; request does not establish purchase, repurchase intent, or current bundle availability."
    },
    {
      "key": "P06",
      "findings": "@jasminesingh1102, TikTok, 5-15: reports product arrived leaked with loose top, requiring opening and cleaning; asks whether oxygen exposure makes it unusable. 12 likes; SKU/version unknown. One detailed arrival-leak/loose-top account; no narrated abandonment or purchase consequence."
    },
    {
      "key": "P07",
      "findings": "@experimentwrld, brand/creator TikTok reply to P06, 5-16: says short-term exposure is not an issue and offers replacement upon email contact. 12 likes. Service offer only; no confirmed contact, shipment, delivery, or independent safety corroboration."
    },
    {
      "key": "P15",
      "findings": "@bmdubs, TikTok, 5-15: plans to reuse an empty container for Lexapro; 150 likes. Resonant reuse intention, not completed reuse or a purchase consequence; container SKU/version unspecified."
    },
    {
      "key": "P17",
      "findings": "@mostlyconceptual, TikTok, 5-16: expresses new brand loyalty, reports an all-Experiment skincare routine and Continuum in the mail; 1 like. Broad brand/joint-routine scope; no packaging attribution or confirmed Continuum receipt/use."
    },
    {
      "key": "P20",
      "findings": "@countryboiiloveyouuuxoxo, TikTok, 5-15: says 'I’m buying everrrrrything'; 7 likes. Broad buying enthusiasm/intention, without explicit completed acquisition, named SKU, or packaging motivation."
    },
    {
      "key": "P21",
      "findings": "@beautybought, TikTok account styled BeautyBought Reviews, 5-17: praises products and packaging one can feel good about; 1 like. Broad approval without specific environmental proof, named SKU, or buying consequence; affiliation unavailable."
    },
    {
      "key": "P26",
      "findings": "@adam_thomas6, TikTok, 5-21: calls packaging great but asks what the product does for skin; 1 like. Packaging approval alongside unresolved efficacy interest, not a skin-performance report; SKU unknown."
    },
    {
      "key": "P27",
      "findings": "@sofieeee120, TikTok, 5-24: asks for a bundle of Continuum and Super Saturated refills; 1 like. Named two-product bundle request, not established joint use, purchase, or explicit repeat-purchase intent."
    },
    {
      "key": "P29",
      "findings": "@allthegr8namesaretaken, TikTok, 5-17: asks how to get the sticker in 'my refill'; 2 likes. Refill/sticker question with unclear mechanics and unspecified SKU; no established defect or purchase consequence."
    },
    {
      "key": "P32",
      "findings": "@josemarbp, TikTok, 5-18: calls it genius and says they might save up; 3 likes. Tentative financially conditioned interest; referent/SKU unspecified, no completed purchase."
    },
    {
      "key": "P38",
      "findings": "@taylorelissa, TikTok, 5-16: calls package cute and cannot wait to try it; 1 like. Aesthetic approval and trial intention, not confirmed use or purchase; SKU unknown."
    },
    {
      "key": "P39",
      "findings": "@morco11111, TikTok, 5-29: praises taking packaging as seriously as formulas; 1 like. General packaging approval, without specific performance, sustainability, or buying testimony."
    },
    {
      "key": "P40",
      "findings": "@danaisabellaaa, TikTok, 5-15: says it is very cute; 1 like. Terse aesthetic approval in packaging context; SKU, use, and purchase consequences unspecified."
    },
    {
      "key": "P42",
      "findings": "@__whitneyjade, TikTok, 5-20: reports receiving theirs that day and excitement on discovering refillability; 1 like. Receipt and previously absent refill awareness, not completed refill use or repurchase intent; SKU/version unknown."
    }
